(a) Application; qualifications. Licenses issued pursuant to this chapter shall not be transferable from the licensee to any other person or entity except by approval of the city manager granted, upon written application, after consideration of such application under all the terms set forth for the issuance of an alcoholic beverage license under this Code, including payment of the applicable investigative and administrative fees provided, and any license fee that may be due.
(b) Partnerships or corporations. In the event of a change of any ownership interest in a business which is owned or operated by a partnership or corporation and for which a license has been issued, the licensee shall report such change to the city commission in writing within five days. The term "change of ownership interest", as used in this subsection means, but is not limited to any change in:
(1) Division of profits and/or losses;
(2) Division of net gross or sales;
(3) Method of paying or amount of rent paid;
(4) Ownership of leased premises, or buildings or land used in the business;
(5) Members of a partnership;
(6) Stockholders of corporate stock; or
(7) Management.
(c) Revocation. If, as a result of any change of ownership interest, the licensee would not qualify under other provisions of this article for the issuance of a license, then the license issued to the licensee shall be subject to revocation and shall not be subject to renewal.
(d) Notice; decision of city manager; fees. Each application for transfer of a license shall have attached thereto a completed copy of the notice of change of interest required by the state revenue commissioner. After receipt of such application, the city manager shall notify the applicant within 30 days of any objection to the transfer. The license shall remain in effect pending approval or disapproval of the transfer. If the transfer is approved, the city manager shall permit the license to be transferred upon payment of a transfer fee equal to one-half the annual license fee. All applications for transfer of a license shall be accompanied by the aforesaid transfer fee, together with an investigative and administrative fee of $300.00. If the transfer is not approved, then the transfer fee will be refunded, but the investigative and administrative fee will not be refunded.
(e) Death of licensee; continuation by qualified executor or administrator. Upon the death of a licensee, the executor or administrator of the licensee's estate may continue to operate under the license for the balance of the calendar year without payment of any additional fee or may delegate the operation of the business to another person if the person operating under the license, whether the executor, administrator, or delegate, would otherwise be qualified as a licensee under the provisions of this article.
(Ord. No. 01-05-01, § 1(24-16), 3-1-2005; Ord. No. 11-09-02, §§ 7, 8, 12-1-09)

